E["npc:archmage-xylem"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Xylem",z="azshara",s="In northern Azshara, Archmage Xylem keeps apart from the world. He pursues arcane research in an isolated tower and receives only those who can aid his studies or settle his vendettas.",h="In northern Azshara, Archmage Xylem keeps apart from the world.",sec={{t="A Recluse Above the Coast",b="Archmage Xylem lives in a secluded spire above northern Azshara's ruined elven coast. No road or trail reaches his sanctuary. His servant Sanath Lim-yo magically carries approved visitors up the cliffs.\n\nAcross Kalimdor, people know Xylem as profoundly eccentric and dangerous to approach. Even fellow scholars treat him with caution. He behaves unlike almost any other human mage.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Against Morphaz",b="Archmage Xylem holds a fierce grudge against the green dragonflight, especially the drake Morphaz. The dragon once swallowed one of Xylem's apprentices whole, along with an arcane shard of immense power.\n\nXylem does not mourn the apprentice. He remains intent on hunting Morphaz and taking the prized artifact from the dragon's belly.",sp=1}},faq={{q="How do you reach Archmage Xylem's tower?",a="No walkable path reaches Archmage Xylem's tower atop a cliff in northern Azshara. Find his servant, Sanath Lim-yo, near the cliffs' base. He can magically carry you to the tower grounds.",al={"get to xylem","reach xylem tower","teleport to xylem","xylem location"}},{q="Who is Archmage Xylem?",a="In northern Azshara, Archmage Xylem lives in an isolated tower and conducts dangerous arcane experiments away from civilization. The eccentric human archmage keeps apart from the world.",al={"who is xylem","archmage xylem lore","xylem background"}},{q="Why does Xylem want the dragon Morphaz dead?",a="Morphaz swallowed one of Archmage Xylem's apprentices whole, along with a shard of immense arcane power. Xylem wants the green drake dead so he can recover the relic from its stomach.",al={"xylem morphaz","why kill morphaz","morphaz shard"}},{q="Why do people say Xylem is dangerous?",a="Jediga and other local contacts warn that Archmage Xylem is unpredictable, detached, and distinctly odd compared with other humans.",al={"is xylem dangerous","xylem crazy","xylem personality"}},{q="Does Xylem belong to the Alliance or the Kirin Tor?",a="Archmage Xylem lives as an independent hermit. He does not serve the Alliance military and will deal with any adventurer willing to do his bidding, whatever their faction.",al={"xylem faction","is xylem alliance","xylem kirin tor"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Xylem's supreme mastery of the arcane. His pursuit of magical power in total isolation brings its own unease.",["faction:Horde"]="Though human, Xylem will parley with Horde champions who can help with his studies.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how Xylem has left human society behind. He lives undisturbed atop the wilds of Azshara."},kw={"arcane","archmage","azshara","morphaz","sanath lim-yo","tower","xylem"},rel={"zone:azshara"},src={"Archmage Xylem"}}
E["npc:azuregos"] = {t="npc",n="Azuregos",z="azshara",s="Along Azshara’s coast, Azuregos keeps watch over Highborne relics. Malygos entrusted their great magic to him, though he would rather study in peace and drive off anyone who breaks his watch.",h="Along Azshara’s coast, Azuregos keeps watch over Highborne relics.",sec={{t="The Guardian of Eldarath",b="Azuregos roams the shores and crags around Eldarath, the ancient ruins he has made his sanctuary. Relics from before the Great Sundering still lie along these shattered coasts. As Malygos’s servant, he keeps their powerful artifacts from careless mortals.\n\nAzuregos does not hide in a dark cave. He patrols the region openly and calls himself its lord of all magic. His humor is often sardonic, yet he fiercely defends Azshara’s treasures from adventurers seeking fame or plunder.",sp=0},{t="A Reluctant Custodian",b="After the War of the Shifting Sands, Azuregos received the Blue Scepter Shard, one fragment of the key needed to break the barrier at the Scarab Wall. Treasure-seekers and would-be heroes came after it, bringing him constant headaches.\n\nAt last, the clever drake rid himself of the shard without ceremony. He fed it to Maws, an empowered minnow. Anyone seeking the shard must now dredge the depths instead of pestering Azuregos.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Azuregos?",a="Azuregos patrols Azshara’s ruins at Malygos’s command. Eccentric and witty, the blue dragon crushes mortals who interrupt his magical studies or covet Eldarath’s treasures.",al={"azuregos lore","who is the blue dragon in azshara","azuregos background"}},{q="Why is Azuregos in Azshara?",a="Azuregos studies and guards the powerful arcane artifacts the ancient Highborne left behind after the Great Sundering. He protects Eldarath’s ruins from reckless plunderers seeking dangerous magic.",al={"why is azuregos here","what is azuregos doing in azshara","azuregos purpose"}},{q="What is his connection to the Scarab Wall?",a="Azuregos received the Blue Scepter Shard, part of the key that can reopen the Scarab Wall. To learn what became of the shard, speak with the dragon.",al={"azuregos scepter shard","azuregos shifting sands","shifting sands shard"},sp=1},{q="Why does his spirit appear in Azshara?",a="The Spirit of Azuregos appears in Azshara near the living dragon and speaks with travelers. No one explains how the spirit and dragon exist side by side.",al={"spirit of azuregos","ghost azuregos","why is azuregos a ghost"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see Azuregos as an agent of the blue dragonflight, devoted to mastering and regulating the arcane. He regards mortal spellcasters as reckless children meddling with forces beyond their understanding.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you can find Azuregos among Eldarath’s shattered ruins, watching over Highborne sorceries that nearly tore Kalimdor apart during the Sundering."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","bay of storms","blue dragon","eldarath","malygos","scepter shard","shifting sands"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:bay-of-storms","subzone:scarab-wall","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:highborne","subzone:bear-s-head","subzone:bitter-reaches"},src={"Azuregos"}}
E["npc:duke-hydraxis"] = {t="npc",n="Duke Hydraxis",z="azshara",s="On a wave-battered islet off Azshara, Duke Hydraxis calls mortals to battle ancient elemental rivals. He leads the Hydraxian Waterlords in service to Neptulon the Tidehunter, with Ragnaros the Firelord his chief foe.",h="On a wave-battered islet off Azshara, Duke Hydraxis calls mortals to battle ancient elemental rivals.",sec={{t="Lord of the Waterlords",b="Duke Hydraxis watches elemental turmoil from a rock northeast of the Ravencrest Monument in Azshara. As emissary of the Hydraxian Waterlords, he acts with purpose amid Azeroth’s hostile and chaotic elementals. He serves Neptulon the Tidehunter and holds water to be the purest and most essential primal force. Now he seeks champions to shift the balance of elemental warfare.",sp=0},{t="The War Against Fire",b="Duke Hydraxis wages his chief campaign against the blazing hosts of Ragnaros the Firelord. He sees the advance of fiery elementals as a blight that must be extinguished.\n\nBefore he trusts mortals with the means to challenge Ragnaros’s stronghold in the Molten Core, they must prove their strength, resilience, and loyalty by slaying hostile elementals across the continents. Those who prove worthy receive the sea’s blessings and the means to douse the sacred flames guarding the Firelord’s domain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Duke Hydraxis be found?",a="You can find Duke Hydraxis on a tiny, isolated island off Azshara’s eastern coast, directly northeast of the Ravencrest Monument.",al={"where is hydraxis","duke hydraxis location","find duke hydraxis","hydraxis map spot"}},{q="Who is Duke Hydraxis aligned with?",a="Duke Hydraxis leads the Hydraxian Waterlords in service to Neptulon the Tidehunter, ruler of the water elementals.",al={"who does hydraxis serve","hydraxis faction","neptulon servant"}},{q="Why is Duke Hydraxis interested in mortal champions?",a="Duke Hydraxis seeks dependable mortal allies to fight rival elemental factions, especially Ragnaros’s fiery forces in Blackrock Mountain.",al={"why does hydraxis need us","what does hydraxis want","hydraxis purpose"}},{q="What is Duke Hydraxis's connection to the Molten Core?",a="Duke Hydraxis directs champions against Ragnaros the Firelord and gives them elemental aids to extinguish the runes and bosses guarding the Molten Core.",al={"hydraxis molten core","hydraxis ragnaros","mc hydraxis"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, meeting an elemental of Duke Hydraxis’s stature offers rare insight into Neptulon’s ancient hierarchy and the enduring rivalries between the elemental planes."},kw={"azshara","duke hydraxis","hydraxian waterlords","hydraxis","molten core","neptulon","ragnaros","water elemental"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:ravencrest-monument","quest:99141"},src={"Duke Hydraxis"}}
E["npc:loramus-thalipedes"] = {t="npc",n="Loramus Thalipedes",z="azshara",s="On a remote isle off Azshara's coast, Loramus Thalipedes keeps three felhounds close. His hunt leads to Razelikh the Defiler in the Blasted Lands.",h="On a remote isle off Azshara's coast, Loramus Thalipedes keeps three felhounds close.",sec={{t="The Blind Hunter of the Isles",b="Southeast of Hetaera's Clutch, Loramus Thalipedes watches from a solitary island. An exile among his kin, he is a demon hunter who endured the agonizing ritual of blinding himself for spectral sight. Raytaf, Shahiar, and Zaman, three towering felhounds, stand around him. From the island, Loramus watches demonic corruption stir across Azeroth and keeps vigil over Azshara's shattered ruins.",sp=0},{t="A Vendetta Across Continents",b="Loramus Thalipedes has set his sights on Razelikh the Defiler, a dreadlord in the Blasted Lands. Ordinary steel cannot kill a cunning demon for good, so Loramus guides travelers through ancient rites. They must gather Azsharite and Razelikh's true name to forge Felbane weapons. These preparations will strip away the dreadlord's wards, bind his true name, and bring Loramus's vendetta to an end.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Loramus Thalipedes?",a="Loramus Thalipedes is a night elf demon hunter living on an isolated island off Azshara's coast. He is devoted to thwarting powerful demons, especially Razelikh the Defiler.",al={"loramus identity","who is the demon hunter in azshara","who is loramus"}},{q="Why is Loramus blindfolded?",a="Like other demon hunters, Loramus gave up his eyes. The ritual exchanged ordinary mortal vision for the spectral sight he needs to detect demonic energies.",al={"why does loramus have no eyes","loramus blind","demon hunter blindfold"}},{q="Why are there felhounds guarding him?",a="Loramus has mastered and bound three powerful felhounds: Raytaf, Shahiar, and Zaman. He turns their predatory instincts against demons rather than the Burning Legion.",al={"loramus felhounds","why does loramus have demons","raytaf shahiar zaman"}},{q="What is his connection to the Blasted Lands?",a="Loramus directs the campaign against Razelikh the Defiler, who rules the heights of the Blasted Lands. He provides the knowledge, rites, and weapons needed to pierce Razelikh's protections.",al={"loramus blasted lands","razelikh quest","why does he care about the blasted lands"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may find demon hunters' ritual self-mutilation and demonic pacts horrifying and worthy of distrust. Your people regard this path as an unforgivable echo of Illidan's betrayal.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may recognize Loramus's controlled felhounds as proof of exceptional mastery over demons. He binds demons to slaughter their own kind."},kw={"azshara","demon hunter","felbane","felhound","hetaera's clutch","loramus","razelikh","thalipedes"},rel={"zone:azshara","zone:blastedlands","subzone:hetaera-s-clutch","topic:night-elf","subzone:altar-of-storms-burning-steppes"},src={"Loramus Thalipedes"}}
E["npc:lord-arkkoroc"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Arkkoroc",z="azshara",s="Along Azshara’s ragged coast, Lord Arkkoroc commands the waters around his ruined temple. Loramus Thalipedes calls him a lesser deity, and the sea giants he calls his sons patrol the shore.",h="Along Azshara’s ragged coast, Lord Arkkoroc commands the waters around his ruined temple.",sec={{t="Lord of the Sunken Coast",b="Lord Arkkoroc holds the ruined Temple of Arkkoran above Azshara’s coast. Loramus Thalipedes, a hermit, regards the colossal sea giant as a lesser deity. His will shapes the waters around the temple. His sons patrol the crags and shallows, keeping his dominion over the shore.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance Against the Deep",b="Lord Arkkoroc has lost many sons beneath the tides. The many-headed hydra Hetaera hunted them along the cliffs and butchered them. For a traveler strong enough to bring him the beast’s heads, Arkkoroc offers valuable knowledge and occult aid.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Arkkoroc?",a="Lord Arkkoroc is a massive sea giant who dwells in the Temple of Arkkoran in Azshara. Loramus Thalipedes regards him as a lesser deity of the seas. Arkkoroc rules the sea giants he calls his sons.",al={"who is arkkoroc","arkkoroc lore","temple sea giant"}},{q="Where can I find Lord Arkkoroc?",a="You can find Lord Arkkoroc among the ruins of the Temple of Arkkoran, on Azshara’s eastern coastline and rocky reefs.",al={"arkkoroc location","where is arkkoroc","find arkkoroc"}},{q="Why does Loramus Thalipedes send adventurers to Arkkoroc?",a="Loramus Thalipedes sends travelers to Arkkoroc for arcane insight about a powerful demon. Arkkoroc holds ancient knowledge, but demands that travelers slay the hydra Hetaera before he shares his secrets.",al={"loramus arkkoroc quest","name of the beast"}},{q="Why is Arkkoroc angry with the hydra Hetaera?",a="Hetaera slaughtered several of Arkkoroc’s sons as they patrolled the coastline. Arkkoroc seeks revenge for his slain kin and demands the hydra’s heads.",al={"why kill hetaera","arkkoroc hydra grudge"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Temple of Arkkoran stands on former Highborne lands. An ancient sea entity now rules over the fallen majesty of old Kalimdor."},kw={"arkkoran","arkkoroc","azshara","hetaera","loramus","lord arkkoroc","sea giant"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","zone:azshara","npc:loramus-thalipedes","topic:naga"},src={"Lord Arkkoroc"}}
E["npc:magus-rimtori"] = {t="npc",n="Magus Rimtori",z="azshara",s="In Azshara, Magus Rimtori leads a blood elf expedition among the ancient ruins. She won passage across Kalimdor by deceiving the Horde, then slaughtered her orcish escort.",h="In Azshara, Magus Rimtori leads a blood elf expedition among the ancient ruins.",sec={{t="A Deadly Deception",b="Magus Rimtori brought high-borne blood elves across the sea to Azshara's ancient shores. To carry them safely through Kalimdor, she charmed and manipulated the orc Belgrom until he agreed to provide an armed escort. Once his soldiers brought her to Azshara, Rimtori turned on her protectors and slaughtered the entire garrison.\n\nHer forces now hold the Thalassian Base Camp. Rimtori ventures into the coastal wilds with elite bodyguards, seeking forgotten magical artifacts.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Ruins",b="Kim'jael, a goblin surveyor betrayed by Rimtori, says she was obsessed with finding an ancient rune. The true purpose of her expedition remains secret, and her ruthless methods have earned her many enemies.\n\nRimtori also betrayed local hirelings. Among the relics left in her camp lies a demonic summoning tome. The Horde she crossed now seeks vengeance for its fallen soldiers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the Horde want Rimtori dead?",a="Rimtori deceived the orc Belgrom into providing an armed escort for her expedition across Kalimdor. After his soldiers brought her safely to Azshara, she betrayed them and slaughtered every orc under his command.",al={"why kill rimtori","belgrom rimtori lore","what did rimtori do to the horde"}},{q="Where can Magus Rimtori be found?",a="Rimtori's expedition holds the Thalassian Base Camp. She roams Azshara's wilderness with her personal blood elf bodyguards, searching for ancient relics.",al={"rimtori location","where is magus rimtori","rimtori azshara location"}},{q="What was Rimtori searching for in Azshara?",a="Kim'jael, the goblin Rimtori hired and then betrayed, says she hunted for an ancient rune. She also sought potent relics, including a Kaldorei tome of summoning.",al={"what does rimtori want","rimtori purpose azshara","rimtori rune"}},{q="Who is Magister Hawkhelm?",a="Magister Hawkhelm is the blood elf officer Rimtori entrusted with commanding and supervising the Thalassian Base Camp while she investigates the surrounding ruins.",al={"hawkhelm","thalassian camp leader","magister hawkhelm rimtori"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Rimtori deceived Belgrom and slaughtered the orc guard sent to escort her. Horde warriors seek to avenge their fallen kin, and she is a priority target.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how far Thalassian magi will go in pursuit of arcane power. They search Kalimdor's ruins and demonic relics."},kw={"azshara","belgrom","blood elf","hawkhelm","kim'jael","magus rimtori","rimtori","thalassian base camp"},rel={"subzone:thalassian-base-camp","zone:azshara","topic:horde","topic:goblin"},src={"Magus Rimtori"}}
E["npc:ogtinc"] = {t="npc",n="Ogtinc",z="azshara",s="High above the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara, Ogtinc guides hunters who seek to test their craft against Kalimdor’s fiercest beasts. He left his tribe to serve nature and became a trusted ally and mentor to the Cenarion Circle.",h="High above the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara, Ogtinc guides hunters who seek to test their craft against...",sec={{t="A Furbolg Apart",b="Ogtinc camps on a bluff southeast of Timbermaw Hold and keeps watch over Azshara’s shattered lands. He left his kin and gave his bow and knowledge of survival to the Cenarion Circle. Many furbolg remain bound to their tribes, while others fell to corruption after the Third War. Ogtinc chose another path.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Hunt",b="Seasoned trackers know Ogtinc for his knowledge of Kalimdor’s wilderness. He tests hunters who have honed their skills across the continents, sending them after rare trophies: courser antlers, sea serpent scales, and parts of green dragonkin. Through these trials, hunters learn to honor the natural world and preserve its balance, rather than take life without thought.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ogtinc?",a="Ogtinc hunts in Azshara and lends his tracking skills and wisdom to the Cenarion Circle. He left his tribe and camps high on the cliffs.",al={"who is ogtinc","ogtinc lore","furbolg in azshara"}},{q="Where can Ogtinc be found?",a="Ogtinc camps on a cliff in Azshara, overlooking the Ruins of Eldarath, southeast of Timbermaw Hold.",al={"where is ogtinc","ogtinc location","how to find ogtinc"}},{q="Why did Ogtinc leave his tribe?",a="Ogtinc left his kin to help the Cenarion Circle preserve nature. His tribal origins are not given, and his clear mind and peaceful manner set him apart from the corrupted tribes elsewhere in northern Kalimdor.",al={"why did ogtinc leave","ogtinc tribe","is ogtinc timbermaw"}},{q="What role does Ogtinc play for hunters?",a="Ogtinc mentors veteran hunters nearing the height of their training. He sends them after fearsome beasts across Kalimdor, from swift coursers to green dragonkin, to test their mastery of the wild.",al={"ogtinc hunter quests","hunter trainer ogtinc","why visit ogtinc"}},{q="Is Ogtinc affiliated with Timbermaw Hold?",a="Ogtinc camps near Timbermaw Hold but works independently with the Cenarion Circle. He is friendly to peaceful travelers, whatever their standing with the Timbermaw tribe.",al={"ogtinc timbermaw","timbermaw reputation ogtinc","is ogtinc friendly"}},{q="Why does Ogtinc watch over the Ruins of Eldarath?",a="Ogtinc watches from high above the Ruins of Eldarath, with a clear view of the wilderness below. Naga, elementals, and lingering magical echoes threaten the balance of the coastal forest.",al={"why is ogtinc in azshara","eldarath ogtinc","ogtinc cliff"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you receive spiritual and practical trials from Ogtinc. He tests your marksmanship and survival against Kalimdor’s deadliest creatures.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can look to Ogtinc as a steadfast partner of the Cenarion Circle. He links the wild wisdom of uncorrupted furbolgs with the druids’ care for nature."},kw={"azshara","cenarion","eldarath","furbolg","hunter","ogtinc","timbermaw"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:furbolg","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:timbermaw-hold"},src={"Ogtinc"}}
E["subzone:bay-of-storms"] = {t="subzone",n="Bay of Storms",z="azshara",s="Storms churn along Azshara’s eastern cliffs, where sailors face a hazardous coast. Ancient ruins, submerged caverns, and dangerous sea beasts fill the bay.",h="Storms churn along Azshara’s eastern cliffs, where sailors face a hazardous coast.",sec={{t="A Tempestuous Coast",b="The Bay of Storms opens onto the Great Sea from Azshara’s eastern coast. Turbulent waters and rocky outcrops shelter dangerous wildlife and ancient aquatic threats. The sunken Temple of Arkkoran lies beneath the waves. Hetaera’s Clutch reefs and Scalebeard’s Cave mark the shore. Casual sailors keep away, leaving the coast to its monsters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Bay of Storms located?",a="The Bay of Storms opens onto the Great Sea from Azshara’s eastern edge, off Kalimdor’s coast.",al={"bay of storms location","where is bay of storms","where is the bay"}},{q="What notable landmarks lie within the bay?",a="The Temple of Arkkoran lies in the bay, with Hetaera’s Clutch reef and Scalebeard’s Cave along its shores.",al={"landmarks in bay of storms","what is in bay of storms","bay of storms points of interest"}},{q="Why is the bay dangerous to navigate?",a="Violent surf, jagged rocks, and hostile aquatic creatures make the bay treacherous for ships. Little coastal civilization is nearby to offer rescue.",al={"is bay of storms safe","why dangerous","bay hazards"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Fishermen seeking rare deep-water catches work the Bay of Storms’ turbulent waters off Kalimdor’s coast."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","great sea","hetaera's clutch","scalebeard's cave","temple of arkkoran"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:hetaera-s-clutch"},src={"Bay of Storms"}}
E["subzone:bear-s-head"] = {t="subzone",n="Bear's Head",z="azshara",s="On Bear's Head in southeastern Azshara, Timbermaw furbolgs keep their outposts beneath the cliffs. Their settlements link to larger homes farther north, while Archmage Xylem studies in a tower above.",h="On Bear's Head in southeastern Azshara, Timbermaw furbolgs keep their outposts beneath the cliffs.",sec={{t="Furbolg Outposts and Cliffside Magic",b="Timbermaw furbolgs keep outposts on Bear's Head, the high ground of southeastern Azshara. Their camps connect north to the larger dens at Ursolan and Timbermaw Hold. Above them, Xylem's Tower stands on the cliffs. Archmage Xylem studies arcane magic there in seclusion with his apprentices and high elven associates. The coast around them remains troubled.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this area called Bear's Head?",a="The Timbermaw furbolg settlements on these hills gave Bear's Head its name. Their camps here serve as southern outposts for the larger homes farther north.",al={"bear's head name origin","why bears head","bears head meaning"}},{q="Which furbolgs live in Bear's Head?",a="Timbermaw furbolgs live in Bear's Head. Many furbolg tribes across Kalimdor fell to demonic corruption, but the Timbermaw have largely resisted the taint. Their settlements remain connected to Ursolan and Timbermaw Hold.",al={"bears head furbolgs","timbermaw in bears head","what furbolg tribe is here"}},{q="What is the tower on the cliffs above Bear's Head?",a="Archmage Xylem owns the tower on the cliffs above Bear's Head. The eccentric human wizard studies in seclusion in Azshara with a handful of apprentices and high elven associates.",al={"tower above bears head","who lives in the tower here","xylem tower"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can seek advanced arcane training from Archmage Xylem. The powerful, eccentric spellcaster's tower overlooks Bear's Head."},kw={"archmage xylem","azshara","bear's head","bears head","furbolg","timbermaw","ursolan"},rel={"zone:azshara","npc:archmage-xylem","topic:furbolg","subzone:timbermaw-hold","subzone:ursolan"},src={"Bear's Head"}}
E["subzone:bitter-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Bitter Reaches",z="azshara",s="Along Azshara’s northeastern cliffs, the Bitter Reaches rise above the Great Sea. Predators roam the heights, and mountain giants hold the northern ridges.",h="Along Azshara’s northeastern cliffs, the Bitter Reaches rise above the Great Sea.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Coastal Frontier",b="The Bitter Reaches rise above the Great Sea along Azshara’s northeastern cliffs. Feral hippogryphs and two-headed chimaeras nest among the heights. Acidic oozes seep through the cold ground, while colossal mountain giants claim the high northern ridges. They drive lesser creatures away and make the frozen approaches perilous for a lone traveler.",sp=0},{t="Flora of the Crags",b="Mountain Silversage grows in sparse clusters on the crags. The rare herb clings to high rock faces and windy perches. Herbalists must avoid the giants and territorial chimaeras to gather it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Bitter Reaches?",a="The Bitter Reaches cover Azshara’s northeastern cliffs and ridges above the bay.",al={"bitter reaches location","where is bitter reaches","bitter reaches azshara"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="Territorial hippogryphs, two-headed chimaeras, and oozes live in the region. Mountain giants roam its northern boundary.",al={"bitter reaches mobs","what lives in bitter reaches","monsters in bitter reaches"}},{q="Why are there mountain giants here?",a="Ancient mountain giants claim the high northern peaks and edges of Azshara. They drive most local wildlife from their territory.",al={"mountain giants azshara","why are giants in bitter reaches"}},{q="What valuable resources grow in the Bitter Reaches?",a="Mountain Silversage grows sparsely on rocky outcrops and ridgelines in the Bitter Reaches.",al={"herbs bitter reaches","bitter reaches gathering"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Mountain Silversage grows in a few places on the wind-battered heights of the Bitter Reaches. You must contend with chimaeras and giants to gather it.",["class:Hunter"]="The cliffside aeries of the Bitter Reaches are hunting grounds for wild hippogryphs and aggressive chimaeras native to this ancient coastline."},kw={"azshara","bitter reaches","chimaera","hippogryph","mountain giant","mountain silversage","ooze"},rel={"zone:azshara"},src={"Bitter Reaches"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Ridge",z="azshara",s="Alliance and Horde positions line the slopes of Forlorn Ridge in southwestern Azshara. The ridge rises above the coast.",h="Alliance and Horde positions line the slopes of Forlorn Ridge in southwestern Azshara.",sec={{t="A Contested Vantage",b="Forlorn Ridge rises above western Azshara, shaped like an ancient volcano long quiet. From its heights, you can see the coast and the ruined elven estates below.\n\nThe ridge commands this stretch of land, so Alliance and Horde forces have built encampments and outposts along its rugged slopes. They watch each other across the bluffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Forlorn Ridge?",a="Forlorn Ridge rises above the wilderness and coastal roads of southwestern Azshara.",al={"where is forlorn ridge","forlorn ridge azshara","what is this mountain"}},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting over this ridge?",a="Forlorn Ridge commands wide views across western Azshara. From its heights, either faction can watch troop movements between the coastal ruins and inland passes. So both have fortified positions on its slopes.",al={"why are there camps here","who controls forlorn ridge","alliance vs horde forlorn ridge"}},{q="Was Forlorn Ridge originally a volcano?",a="Forlorn Ridge's rugged shape suggests it may once have been a volcano. It has long been quiet and overgrown.",al={"is forlorn ridge a volcano","volcano in azshara"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you can watch Horde movements spilling eastward from the Barrens and Ashenvale. Forlorn Ridge gives you early warning and a view of the field.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use footholds along Forlorn Ridge to help secure Azshara's rugged borderlands just north of Durotar against Alliance incursions."},kw={"azshara","forlorn ridge","fortifications","mountain","ruins of eldarath","volcano"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:horde","topic:alliance","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath"},src={"Forlorn Ridge"}}
E["subzone:haldarr-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Haldarr Encampment",z="azshara",s="In western Azshara, Haldarr satyrs hold a corrupted outpost northeast of Shadowsong Shrine and southwest of Valormok. Their camp blights ancient elven ruins, and the injured Night Elf Sentinel Keldara Sunblade lies among them.",h="In western Azshara, Haldarr satyrs hold a corrupted outpost northeast of Shadowsong Shrine and southwest of...",sec={{t="A Den of Demon-Spawn",b="Broken stones mark the Haldarr satyrs’ camp in western Azshara. These twisted creatures descend from the Highborne and were cursed by demonic corruption during the Sundering. They hunt and harass anyone crossing the autumn forests. Their crowded settlement threatens the Horde forces at nearby Valormok and the dwindling Night Elf sentinels watching the region.",sp=0},{t="The Captured Sentinel",b="Sentinel Keldara Sunblade lies injured among the satyrs, deep in enemy territory. No account tells why she remains there.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Haldarr Encampment?",a="Haldarr satyrs control a corrupted settlement in western Azshara, northeast of Shadowsong Shrine and southwest of Valormok.",al={"haldarr encampment lore","what is haldarr","who lives in haldarr encampment"}},{q="Who are the Haldarr?",a="The Haldarr are a vicious sect of satyrs living in Azshara. Like all satyrs, they descend from ancient Night Elves who embraced demonic pacts during the War of the Ancients. They were cursed into goat-legged fiends who serve the remnants of the Burning Legion’s will.",al={"haldarr satyrs","who are the satyrs here"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Keldara Sunblade?",a="Sentinel Keldara Sunblade is a wounded Night Elf Sentinel inside the Haldarr Encampment, surrounded by hostile satyrs. No account tells why she is there.",al={"keldara sunblade","injured night elf","who is the captive here"}},{q="Why is this camp dangerous to nearby travelers?",a="Aggressive satyrs crowd the camp and threaten the surrounding paths. They endanger Horde operations from Valormok and any wandering scouts in the area.",al={"is haldarr dangerous","why clear haldarr"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the Haldarr satyrs remain a shameful reminder of the ancient Highborne’s descent into demonic madness.",["faction:Horde"]="Just southwest of Valormok, this dense nest of demons threatens Horde scouts and supply lines pushing across Azshara’s cliffs."},kw={"azshara","encampment","haldarr","keldara sunblade","satyr","shadowsong shrine","valormok"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:satyr","subzone:valormok","subzone:shadowsong-shrine"},src={"Haldarr Encampment"}}
E["subzone:hetaera-s-clutch"] = {t="subzone",n="Hetaera's Clutch",z="azshara",s="Hetaera's brood now nests among the drowned ruins beneath Azshara's Bay of Storms. Once, night elves came to this temple to worship Elune.",h="Hetaera's brood now nests among the drowned ruins beneath Azshara's Bay of Storms.",sec={{t="A Drowned Sanctuary",b="Before the Great Sundering broke ancient Kalimdor apart, night elves came to this temple to worship Elune. The sanctuary sank beneath the Bay of Storms, where its pillars and halls have rested under the sea for ten thousand years. Now the tides cover every sign of worship, and the Kaldorei ruins lie below the waves.",sp=0},{t="Domain of the Broodmother",b="Hetaera makes her nest in the drowned sanctuary. The massive hydra has many heads and stalks the nearby coastal waters and rocky isles. Her offspring, the Spawn of Hetaera, prowl the ruined arches and corridors. They attack any surface-dweller bold enough to dive into the bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Hetaera's Clutch originally built for?",a="Before sinking, Hetaera's Clutch was a temple dedicated to Elune, the moon goddess. It was built at the height of the ancient night elven empire and sank into the ocean during the Great Sundering.",al={"what is hetaeras clutch","what was this temple","hetaera clutch lore"}},{q="Where is Hetaera's Clutch located?",a="Hetaera's Clutch rests deep beneath the Bay of Storms, off Azshara's jagged southern coast.",al={"where is hetaeras clutch","hetaera clutch location","how to find hetaera clutch"}},{q="Who is Hetaera?",a="Hetaera is a three-headed hydra that prowls Azshara's waters. Her children infest the sunken temple, while she is usually found swimming just north of the Clutch or basking on nearby offshore islands.",al={"who is hetaera","where is hetaera","what is hetaera"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the submerged ruins?",a="Hetaera's brood inhabits the drowned halls. These vicious aquatic hydras defend their nesting site against intruders who swim too close.",al={"what mobs are in hetaeras clutch","what lives in hetaera clutch"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see the drowned sanctuary of Elune, now a hydra nest, as a reminder of the civilization lost in the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid exploring the Bay of Storms, beware the hydras claiming this ancient sanctuary. They are hostile to trespassers."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","elune","hetaera","hetaera's clutch","hetaeras clutch","hydra","sunken temple","temple of elune"},rel={"subzone:bay-of-storms","zone:azshara","topic:elune"},src={"Hetaera's Clutch"}}
E["subzone:horizon-scout"] = {t="subzone",n="Horizon Scout",z="azshara",s="Off Azshara’s southern coast, Horizon Scout lies sunk in the Ruined Reaches. Captain Vanessa Beltis is stranded ashore, and part of her crew is trapped below the waves.",h="Off Azshara’s southern coast, Horizon Scout lies sunk in the Ruined Reaches.",sec={{t="Trapped on the Ocean Floor",b="Horizon Scout lies wrecked among the Ruined Reaches’ shoals off Azshara’s jagged coast. Captain Vanessa Beltis reached a nearby peninsula, but part of her crew went down with the hull. They still live because Roland Geardabbler, a gnome, sustains a spell of water breathing inside the wreck.\n\nHostile aquatic predators and predatory naga patrol the waters. The sailors are trapped in the forward compartments and cannot reach the surface alone.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Ambush",b="A shard of raw Azsharite lies in Horizon Scout’s forward stairwell. The mineral is mysterious and found only on these shores. Spitelash naga prowl the Ruined Reaches and likely struck the ship to seize artifacts or resources from its expedition.\n\nThe vessel sank, leaving its survivors unable to escape with any secrets or treasures the coast holds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Horizon Scout located?",a="Horizon Scout lies submerged on the ocean floor in the Ruined Reaches, off Azshara’s southern coast.",al={"horizon scout location","where is horizon scout","find horizon scout"}},{q="How is the crew still alive underwater?",a="Roland Geardabbler, a gnome, continually channels water breathing inside the sunken hull, keeping the trapped crew alive in breathable air.",al={"how are they breathing","why crew not dead","roland geardabbler aura"}},{q="Who is Captain Vanessa Beltis?",a="Captain Vanessa Beltis commands Horizon Scout. She reached Azshara’s southern peninsula with a few stranded survivors, while other sailors remain trapped in the hull.",al={"vanessa beltis","horizon scout captain","ship captain"}},{q="What caused the Horizon Scout to sink?",a="Spitelash naga almost certainly ambushed and sank Horizon Scout. A shard of raw Azsharite on the lower deck suggests they sought mineral riches or artifacts gathered by the expedition.",al={"why did horizon scout sink","who sank horizon scout","what happened to the ship"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see the surviving crew depend on Roland Geardabbler’s sustained spell to breathe inside the flooded hull.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find Horizon Scout’s crew divided between shore and sea after a disastrous voyage through Azshara’s perilous waters."},kw={"azshara shipwreck","azsharite","horizon scout","roland geardabbler","ruined reaches","spitelash","vanessa beltis"},rel={"subzone:ruined-reaches","zone:azshara","topic:naga","subzone:faldir-s-cove"},src={"Horizon Scout"}}
E["subzone:jagged-reef"] = {t="subzone",n="Jagged Reef",z="azshara",s="Along Azshara’s northern coast, ships find no safe passage through Jagged Reef. Sandy beaches meet stone spurs and churning surf, where hydras, makrura, and murlocs prowl.",h="Along Azshara’s northern coast, ships find no safe passage through Jagged Reef.",sec={{t="A Perilous Shoreline",b="Jagged Reef cuts along Azshara’s northern edge. Broken cliffs and jutting stones divide sandy shores into quiet inlets. Beneath the water, crags and shifting shallows make the passage deadly to ships.\n\nOn shore, hydras and makrura prowl the surf. Murlocs search the tides for scraps and unwary prey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Jagged Reef located?",a="Jagged Reef runs along Azshara’s northern shore, where beaches, rocky spurs, and small ocean inlets meet.",al={"jagged reef location","where is jagged reef"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Jagged Reef?",a="Hydras, makrura, and murlocs prowl the shallows and sandy beaches of Jagged Reef.",al={"what lives here","jagged reef mobs","monsters in jagged reef"}},{q="Can ships navigate the waters around the Jagged Reef?",a="No. Underwater rocks and shifting shallows make the waters around Jagged Reef too dangerous for ships.",al={"can boats sail here","jagged reef shipping"}},{q="Are there any settlements along the reef?",a="No civilized settlements lie along Jagged Reef. Murloc encampments are the only organized presence on the shore, apart from passing explorers or hunters.",al={"towns near jagged reef","who lives at jagged reef"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can study or tame the hydras and shoreline crustaceans on Jagged Reef’s exposed northern beaches."},kw={"azshara","beach","coast","hydras","jagged reef","makrura","murlocs","shallows"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:murloc"},src={"Jagged Reef"}}
E["subzone:lake-mennar"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Mennar",z="azshara",s="At Lake Mennar, blue dragonspawn guard the freshwater amid Azshara’s shattered ruins. The shores stay strangely serene, and blue dragons gather here in numbers rarely seen beyond Northrend.",h="At Lake Mennar, blue dragonspawn guard the freshwater amid Azshara’s shattered ruins.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary for the Blue Dragonflight",b="Lake Mennar draws the blue dragonflight into Azshara’s ancient, broken landscape. Few places on Kalimdor hold so many blue dragons; Mazthoril in Winterspring is another. Blue dragonspawn patrol the ridges and approaches, guarding the basin’s waters. Beyond their ring of sentries, the lake remains strangely serene, shielded from the arcane turmoil and roaming beast packs found across the peninsula.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there blue dragons at Lake Mennar?",a="Lake Mennar is one of the blue dragonflight’s few gathering grounds on Kalimdor outside Mazthoril in Winterspring. Dragonspawn patrol the perimeter, guarding the basin and keeping intruders from their brood.",al={"why blue dragons here","who lives at lake mennar","blue dragonflight lake mennar"}},{q="Is Lake Mennar dangerous to visit?",a="Blue dragonkin and whelps patrol the surrounding ridges and approaches. Inside the basin, the water and immediate shoreline are surprisingly peaceful if you pass the guards.",al={"is lake mennar safe","enemies at lake mennar"}},{q="How does Lake Mennar connect to other blue dragon roosts?",a="On Kalimdor, Lake Mennar and Mazthoril in Winterspring are the blue flight’s main known territories. Both are rare outposts far south of the flight’s ancestral home in Northrend.",al={"connection to mazthoril","lake mennar winterspring"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find the blue dragons guarding Lake Mennar of great interest, for they are stewards of the world’s arcane energies."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","blue dragonflight","dragonspawn","lake mennar","mazthoril","whelps"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:mazthoril","npc:azuregos","zone:winterspring"},src={"Lake Mennar"}}
E["subzone:ravencrest-monument"] = {t="subzone",n="Ravencrest Monument",z="azshara",s="On southern Azshara’s windswept cliffs, Ravencrest Monument lies broken above the Great Sea. Hostile Spitelash naga stalk the remains of the ancient night elven colossus.",h="On southern Azshara’s windswept cliffs, Ravencrest Monument lies broken above the Great Sea.",sec={{t="Ruins of a Colossus",b="Southeast of the Ruins of Eldarath, Ravencrest Monument rises above the ocean. The ancient colossus once showed the skill of Kaldorei stoneworkers. Now only its enormous legs remain, fixed to a stone base. Its torso and head lie in fragments, buried in the cliff dirt or lost beneath the waves.\n\nTo reach this remote coast, you must cross Azshara’s mainland bridges. Steep, rocky drops block any approach from the sea.",sp=0},{t="A Forgotten Legacy",b="Some scholars believe Ravencrest Monument honors Lord Kur'talos Ravencrest, the famed noble who rallied and led the night elven host after Zin-Azshari fell in the War of the Ancients. Its closeness to ancient Eldarath and the surviving stonework leave its origins uncertain.\n\nSpitelash naga now claim the cliff. They defend the fallen monument with fierce aggression, where pilgrims or night elven caretakers once might have stood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ravencrest Monument?",a="Ravencrest Monument is a ruined night elven colossus on a coastal promontory in southern Azshara. Only its enormous stone legs remain upright; the rest lies shattered across the clifftop.",al={"ravencrest statue","what is this statue","giant legs azshara"}},{q="Who was the monument built to honor?",a="The monument’s name points to House Ravencrest, best known for Lord Kur'talos Ravencrest, who led mortal resistance against the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients. Since the monument stands near Eldarath, it may honor Kur'talos or an earlier ancestor from before the Great Sundering.",al={"who is ravencrest","who is the statue of","kurtalos ravencrest"}},{q="How do you reach the monument?",a="You must cross southern Azshara by land, using stone bridges near the Ruins of Eldarath to reach the promontory. Sheer cliffs block any approach from the sea.",al={"how to get to ravencrest monument","ravencrest path","ravencrest access"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the monument today?",a="Spitelash naga inhabit the clifftop and surrounding terraces, making the ancient ruins perilous to explore alone.",al={"what lives here","monument enemies","azshara naga"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Ravencrest Monument as a reminder of the ancient Kaldorei Empire and the Ravencrest noble line. The family’s resistance during the War of the Ancients saved Azeroth from demonic annihilation.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you hear the weight of the Ravencrest name in the tale of Kur'talos Ravencrest, foremost general of the mortal forces during the Burning Legion’s catastrophic invasion."},kw={"azshara","colossus","eldarath","kurtalos ravencrest","ravencrest","ravencrest monument","spitelash","statue"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","topic:night-elf","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:naga","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Ravencrest Monument"}}
E["subzone:ruined-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruined Reaches",z="azshara",s="Along Azshara’s southern coast, the Ruined Reaches lie beneath the mainland cliffs. Wrecked ships and dangerous shallows mark the beaches, while predators haunt the surf and a small gnomish outpost watches from above.",h="Along Azshara’s southern coast, the Ruined Reaches lie beneath the mainland cliffs.",sec={{t="A Battered Coast",b="The Ruined Reaches stretch along southern Azshara, just north of Durotar. Rocky inlets and cliff faces break up the sand, where wreckage washes ashore. Like the Jagged Reef farther north, hidden shallows make sea travel perilous. Many ships have broken against this coast.\n\nHostile creatures roam both beach and water. Territorial murlocs, vicious hydras, and armored makrura make crossing the shore as dangerous as crossing the surf.",sp=0},{t="The Gadgetspring Outpost",b="A steep trail climbs from the beaches to a gnomish workshop high on the western cliff. Blimo and Jubie Gadgetspring keep the outpost, selling engineering components and general trade goods to travelers. An elevator leads up to private quarters with three beds. Who, if anyone, sleeps in the third bunk remains unknown.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Ruined Reaches located?",a="The Ruined Reaches follow Azshara’s southern coast, along the northern edge of Durotar. Beaches, coastal inlets, and cliffs lie beneath the mainland bluffs.",al={"ruined reaches location","where is ruined reaches","how to get to ruined reaches"}},{q="What threats inhabit this stretch of coast?",a="Hostile creatures prowl the beaches and shallow waters. Aggressive murloc tribes, multi-headed hydras, and makrura haunt the tidal flats.",al={"ruined reaches mobs","what lives here","monsters in ruined reaches"}},{q="Who lives in the gnomish structure on the cliffs?",a="Blimo and Jubie Gadgetspring live and work in the cliffside outpost. Their small shop sells engineering parts and trade supplies to travelers on the coast.",al={"gnomes in ruined reaches","gadgetspring house","who lives in the gnome house"}},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks here?",a="Like the nearby Jagged Reef, this coast hides shallow rocks and other hazards. Ships can strike them unaware and break against the cliffs.",al={"shipwrecks in azshara","why are ships wrecked here","ruined reaches wrecks"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Blimo and Jubie Gadgetspring’s remote workshop offers useful parts and supplies to engineers exploring Azshara’s wilds.",["race:Gnome"]="A gnomish homestead high on Azshara’s hostile cliffs shows the resourcefulness of gnomes far from Ironforge."},kw={"azshara","blimo gadgetspring","durotar","jagged reef","jubie gadgetspring","makrura","murloc","ruined reaches"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:jagged-reef","zone:durotar","topic:murloc"},src={"Ruined Reaches"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-eldarath"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Eldarath",z="azshara",s="Naga overrun the Ruins of Eldarath along Azshara’s rocky bluffs. Once a Highborne city of arcane study, its surviving plazas and temples still draw scholars and adventurers seeking ancient tablets and relics.",h="Naga overrun the Ruins of Eldarath along Azshara’s rocky bluffs.",sec={{t="A Shattered Highborne Bastion",b="Before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, Eldarath flourished as a night elven city. Highborne mages gathered there and carved their deepest arcane insights and fundamental magical rules into grand stone tablets.\n\nThey left the tablets in public squares for their peers to study. The Sundering sank much of the city into the Bay of Storms. Modern night elves have shunned the surviving ruins along the eastern cliffs for millennia, while salt spray and ivy slowly claim them.",sp=0},{t="Naga Rule and Forgotten Relics",b="Vicious naga have risen from the sea and seized Eldarath’s shattered streets. Warlords command them from nearby sanctuaries, including the Temple of Zin-Malor. Yet danger has not kept outsiders away.\n\nThe Explorers' League sends Alliance adventurers into the broken courtyards to take rubbings of the ancient tablets. Whispers of lost treasures and lingering magic have also drawn the blue dragon Azuregos to the surrounding wilderness. Beneath the cracked flagstones, secrets of immense power may still lie buried.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Eldarath before it fell into ruins?",a="Before the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, Eldarath flourished as a night elven city populated by the Highborne. It was a center of arcane study and a fortified haven until the Sundering devastated it.",al={"what was eldarath","eldarath history","eldarath origin"}},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Eldarath today?",a="Hostile naga now overrun the ruins and hold the crumbling plazas and nearby structures as coastal strongholds. Warlords such as Krellian command them from places like the Temple of Zin-Malor.",al={"who lives in eldarath","what is in eldarath","eldarath mobs"}},{q="Why do scholars and explorers travel to Eldarath?",a="Scholars seek the ancient stone tablets left by Highborne mages. The public tablets record fundamental rules of arcane magic and long-lost research. Groups such as the Dwarven Explorers' League send scouts to secure rubbings.",al={"why go to eldarath","eldarath quests","what is at eldarath"}},{q="Why is the blue dragon Azuregos roaming near the ruins?",a="Azuregos is drawn to the ancient arcane power lingering along Azshara’s coast. Rumors say powerful relics from before the Sundering may remain hidden in or around the ruins, perhaps even vials touched by the ancient Well of Eternity.",al={"why is azuregos here","azuregos eldarath","blue dragon in azshara"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you find a solemn place of study in Eldarath. Tablets across its plazas preserve foundational arcane theories carved by gifted Highborne sorcerers before their empire fell.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Highborne’s hubris and the Sundering in these sun-bleached ruins. Modern Kaldorei long avoided them, and naga now defile the ruins."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","eldarath","explorers' league","highborne","kaldorei","naga","sundering","tablets"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:temple-of-zin-malor","subzone:bay-of-storms","npc:azuregos","topic:highborne","topic:naga","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Eldarath"}}
E["subzone:shadowsong-shrine"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowsong Shrine",z="azshara",s="In western Azshara, Shadowsong Shrine lies in haunted ruin near the Ashenvale border. Ancient Highborne spirits haunt the hillside sanctuary. Its name recalls Maiev Shadowsong, though its tie to her bloodline remains a mystery.",h="In western Azshara, Shadowsong Shrine lies in haunted ruin near the Ashenvale border.",sec={{t="A Haunted Legacy",b="Shadowsong Shrine crowns a hill above Azshara’s shattered lands, its stones lost beneath overgrowth. Highborne ghosts wander the ruins and try to kill mortals who enter their domain.\n\nThe shrine bears the name of Maiev Shadowsong, the warden of Illidan Stormrage. Time has erased whether it honors her family or predates the Sundering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shadowsong Shrine?",a="Shadowsong Shrine lies in crumbled ruin on a hill in western Azshara. Hostile Highborne spirits haunt the old night elf sanctuary.",al={"what is this place","shadowsong shrine info","ruins on the hill azshara"}},{q="Who is the shrine named after?",a="Shadowsong Shrine shares its name with Maiev Shadowsong, the warden who held Illidan Stormrage captive. Whether the shrine honors Maiev or her family is unknown.",al={"maiev shadowsong","why shadowsong"}},{q="Why is the shrine haunted?",a="The Great Sundering devastated Shadowsong Shrine ten thousand years ago. Highborne spirits slain in the cataclysm remain bound to the stones, mad and hostile toward the living.",al={"why are there ghosts here","highborne ghosts azshara","ghosts at shadowsong shrine"}},{q="Where is the shrine located?",a="Shadowsong Shrine sits on a hill in western Azshara, east of the Ashenvale border and near Talrendis Point.",al={"where is shadowsong shrine","shadowsong shrine location","how to find shadowsong shrine"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the respect Maiev Shadowsong commands. Tormented Highborne ghosts haunt the shrine that bears her name."},kw={"azshara","ghosts","highborne","maiev","ruins","shadowsong","shrine"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:highborne","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:alliance"},src={"Shadowsong Shrine"}}
E["subzone:shattered-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Shattered Strand",z="azshara",s="Waves batter Shattered Strand along Azshara’s northern coast, where ancient ruins overlook the shore. Sea beasts and aquatic tribes prowl the shallows.",h="Waves batter Shattered Strand along Azshara’s northern coast, where ancient ruins overlook the shore.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coastline",b="The Shattered Strand runs along the northern edge of the Bay of Storms. Rocky beaches and tidal shallows teem with danger. Sea giants, hydras, and snapping makrura roam beside coastal murloc camps. Ruined elven buildings overlook the waves, including the ancient Temple of Arkkoran and the lone Tower of Eldara. Travelers who descend Azshara’s cliffs reach an isolated coast held by deadly amphibious creatures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Shattered Strand located?",a="The Shattered Strand runs along the northern coast of the Bay of Storms in eastern Azshara, beneath the zone’s high cliffs.",al={"shattered strand location","where is shattered strand","shattered strand map"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Shattered Strand?",a="Hydras, sea giants, makrura, and hostile murlocs prowl the shore and tidal flats.",al={"shattered strand mobs","what lives on shattered strand","shattered strand beasts"}},{q="What notable ruins can be found along the beach?",a="The ancient Temple of Arkkoran and the nearby Tower of Eldara overlook the bay.",al={"shattered strand ruins","buildings on shattered strand","landmarks shattered strand"}},{q="Is the Shattered Strand safe for casual exploration?",a="No. The isolated beach lies below sheer cliffs and teems with predatory aquatic beasts and powerful giants, making a quick escape difficult.",al={"is shattered strand dangerous","shattered strand level"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test yourself against hydras and other coastal beasts along this wild shore, or study the predatory wildlife of Kalimdor’s coast."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","hydras","makrura","murlocs","sea giants","shattered strand","temple of arkkoran","tower of eldara"},rel={"subzone:bay-of-storms","zone:azshara","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:tower-of-eldara","topic:murloc"},src={"Shattered Strand"}}
E["subzone:southfury-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Southfury River",z="azshara",s="Mount Hyjal's waters run south through central Kalimdor in the Southfury River. Along the way, the river divides Azshara from Ashenvale and Durotar from the Barrens, then reaches the Great Sea near Ratchet.",h="Mount Hyjal's waters run south through central Kalimdor in the Southfury River.",sec={{t="A Vital Natural Divide",b="The Southfury River starts high on Mount Hyjal and rushes through central Kalimdor. Its waters divide Ashenvale from Azshara, then Durotar from the Barrens. Only a few bridges cross its swift current. One guards Orgrimmar's rear gates, while another links Durotar to the Barrens. Near Ratchet, the river plunges over a waterfall into the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="Strategic Importance",b="The Southfury gives the Horde a barrier and a route through the region. It shields Durotar's western approaches, including Orgrimmar, from immediate ground assault. Its waters also carry fresh mountain runoff through dry country. Just north of the western crossing into Orgrimmar, Ashenvale, Azshara, Durotar, and the Barrens meet. Holding the river keeps supply lines between Orgrimmar and outlying Horde settlements intact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Southfury River start and end?",a="The Southfury River begins high on Mount Hyjal and ends in a waterfall that pours into the Great Sea northeast of Ratchet. It flows south between Ashenvale, Azshara, Durotar, and the Barrens.",al={"source of southfury river","where does southfury go","southfury mouth"}},{q="Which zones does the river border?",a="The Southfury River divides Ashenvale from Azshara in the north, then the Barrens from Durotar in the south. North of Orgrimmar's western bridge, all four territories meet along the riverbanks.",al={"what zones are on southfury","southfury border"}},{q="Where can travelers cross the Southfury River?",a="Travelers can cross the Southfury River by bridges linking Azshara to Ashenvale, reaching Orgrimmar's rear gates, and connecting Durotar with the Barrens.",al={"southfury bridges","how to cross southfury","bridges over southfury"}},{q="Why is the river important to Orgrimmar?",a="The Southfury River shields the western flank of Orgrimmar and Durotar. It also carries fresh mountain water through a dry region.",al={"southfury orgrimmar","why horde cares about southfury"}},{q="What is the Southfury River?",a="The Southfury River is the most prominent waterway in central Kalimdor. Flowing south from the heights of Mount Hyjal, its swift, wide waters carve natural borders between the forests of Ashenvale and the ruins of Azshara before cutting down to divide Durotar from the Barrens. It ultimately empties into the Great Sea through a cascading waterfall just northeast of the goblin port of Ratchet.",al={"what is southfury river","southfury river overview","southfury river lore"},it="place",add="dbc3f3f2"},{q="Is the Southfury River dangerous?",a="The river itself is a swiftly flowing torrent with perilous, plunging waterfalls where it tumbles from Mount Hyjal and empties into the sea. Beyond the treacherous current, the lands on either side are rife with conflict and prowling beasts, making any unguided crossing far riskier than sticking to the fortified bridges.",al={"is southfury river dangerous","southfury river threats","southfury dangers"},it="danger",add="4c95fcc0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the Southfury River guards Durotar's western edge and links the capital to the heart of the Barrens."},kw={"ashenvale","azshara","barrens","durotar","hyjal","orgrimmar","ratchet","southfury","southfury river"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:ashenvale","zone:azshara","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:ratchet","topic:horde"},src={"Southfury River"}}
E["subzone:southridge-beach"] = {t="subzone",n="Southridge Beach",z="azshara",s="Along Azshara’s southern coast, Southridge Beach borders the turbulent Bay of Storms. Its broken ruins now shelter naga, murlocs, and towering sea giants.",h="Along Azshara’s southern coast, Southridge Beach borders the turbulent Bay of Storms.",sec={{t="A Drowned Shoreline",b="On Southridge Beach, the southern shore meets the turbulent Bay of Storms. Thousands of years ago, this coast belonged to Eldarath, a magnificent Highborne city. The Great Sundering broke the land and drowned most of its palaces. Crumbling marble pillars and weathered stone pavilions still dot the sand. Spitelash naga, prowling makrura, vicious hydras, and scavenging murloc tribes now contest the shore. Even massive sea giants sometimes wander ashore from the deep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Southridge Beach located?",a="Southridge Beach lies in central Azshara, along the southern edge of the turbulent Bay of Storms, beneath the mainland cliffs.",al={"southridge beach location","where is southridge beach","azshara southridge beach"}},{q="What ruins are scattered along the beach?",a="The columns and arches on the sand are the outer ruins of Eldarath, a great Highborne night elf city shattered and flooded in the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago.",al={"southridge beach ruins","eldarath ruins beach","what are the ruins here"}},{q="What creatures live on Southridge Beach?",a="Naga, primitive murlocs, armored makrura, and dangerous hydras occupy the shore, and sea giants sometimes roam there.",al={"mobs on southridge beach","enemies southridge beach","what lives here"}},{q="Why are there so many naga here?",a="Naga have risen from the ocean depths to reclaim the ruins of their former civilization across Azshara. They have established a firm military presence along the Bay of Storms beaches.",al={"why naga on beach","naga southridge beach","azshara naga"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Southridge Beach’s ruined architecture as a reminder of the heights of ancient Highborne civilization and its tragic fall in the Great Sundering."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","eldarath","makrura","murloc","naga","sea giant","southridge beach"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:bay-of-storms","topic:naga","topic:murloc"},src={"Southridge Beach"}}
E["subzone:temple-of-arkkoran"] = {t="subzone",n="Temple of Arkkoran",z="azshara",s="On Azshara’s northeastern cliffs, the Temple of Arkkoran looks out over the Shattered Strand. Elune’s old sanctuary now belongs to Arkkoroc and his aquatic thralls.",h="On Azshara’s northeastern cliffs, the Temple of Arkkoran looks out over the Shattered Strand.",sec={{t="A Consecrated Ruin Claimed by the Sea",b="Elune, the moon goddess, was once honored at the Temple of Arkkoran. The Sundering shattered the ancient night elf empire and left the temple in ruin. Now tidal monstrosities crowd its marble steps and broken colonnades. Arkkoroc rules from the highest level, with loyal makrura and vicious murlocs at his side. Together, they defend the nearby coast from land-dwelling intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Temple of Arkkoran originally built for?",a="Night elves built the Temple of Arkkoran as a sanctuary to Elune. The Great Sundering ruined it and the coastal civilization around it.",al={"temple of arkkoran history","who built temple of arkkoran","what is this temple"}},{q="Who is Arkkoroc?",a="Arkkoroc is a powerful sea giant who has made the former night elf temple his home. From its highest platform, he commands the shore and its coastal beasts.",al={"who is arkkoroc","arkkoroc sea giant","who rules arkkoran"}},{q="What creatures guard the temple grounds?",a="Aggressive makrura and murlocs patrol the temple and its terraces, including Arkkoran clackers, pincers, and muckdwellers. Hydras and other sea giants live on the Shattered Strand beaches.",al={"temple of arkkoran mobs","what lives at temple of arkkoran","enemies at temple of arkkoran"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Elune’s sacred house overrun by makrura and sea giants. Its ruin recalls the splendor lost ten thousand years ago.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can still see ancient symbols of Elune among the weathered stones. No divine communion remains in these sea-battered ruins."},kw={"arkkoroc","azshara","elune","makrura","murloc","sea giant","shattered strand","temple of arkkoran"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:shattered-strand","topic:elune","topic:murloc"},src={"Temple of Arkkoran"}}
E["subzone:temple-of-zin-malor"] = {t="subzone",n="Temple of Zin-Malor",z="azshara",s="Spitelash naga hold the Temple of Zin-Malor in the Ruins of Eldarath. Warlord Krellian commands them from this ancient night elven sanctuary in Azshara.",h="Spitelash naga hold the Temple of Zin-Malor in the Ruins of Eldarath.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Moon",b="Before the Great Sundering, the Temple of Zin-Malor rang with worship of Elune. Its graceful stonework recalls the nearby Temple of Arkkoran and the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, both built in the old night elven style. Now the marble lies weathered and broken. Spitelash naga have claimed the holy grounds and made them a stronghold for their forces.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Crystal",b="The Crystal of Zin-Malor once rested in the temple. Long ago, it was carried away to Kel'Theril in Winterspring.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls the Temple of Zin-Malor today?",a="Spitelash naga occupy the Temple of Zin-Malor today. Their regional leader, Warlord Krellian, lives within its walls.",al={"who is at zin-malor","who lives in zin malor","who is the boss in zin malor"}},{q="What was the temple used for originally?",a="Ancient night elves built the temple before the Great Sundering as a sacred place to worship Elune, the moon goddess.",al={"who built zin-malor","what was zin-malor"}},{q="Why does it look so much like the temple in Darnassus?",a="The Temple of Zin-Malor and the nearby Temple of Arkkoran share the old night elven style seen in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"darnassus temple resemblance","architecture of zin-malor"}},{q="What is the Crystal of Zin-Malor?",a="The Crystal of Zin-Malor is an ancient magical relic that once rested in the temple. Long ago, residents of Kel'Theril carried it away to Winterspring.",al={"where is the crystal of zin malor","zin malor crystal"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see the Highborne era in Zin-Malor's ruins and the naga's corruption of ground once sacred to Elune.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can find Elune's worship in these stones and sanctuary layouts like those still kept by the sisterhoods in Darnassus."},kw={"arkkoran","azshara","crystal of zin-malor","eldarath","krellian","spitelash","zin-malor"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:elune","topic:naga","topic:highborne","zone:azshara","zone:winterspring"},src={"Temple of Zin-Malor"}}
E["subzone:thalassian-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Thalassian Base Camp",z="azshara",s="On a ridge in northern Azshara, the blood elf expedition at Thalassian Base Camp digs through ancient ruins for arcane relics. Their pact with the Horde is broken.",h="On a ridge in northern Azshara, the blood elf expedition at Thalassian Base Camp digs through ancient ruins...",sec={{t="A Fractured Accord",b="East of Ursolan, the blood elf expedition once promised not to threaten travelers from Orgrimmar. Magus Rimtori offered the Horde a share of any magical riches in return for supplies, funding, and an armed escort through Azshara’s wildlands.\n\nOnce the camp was fortified and the first relics were recovered from the elven ruins, Rimtori broke the pact and drove away the Horde emissaries. She now searches deeper reaches with an armed retinue. Magister Hawkhelm guards the ridge and camp against retribution.",sp=0},{t="Dust and Demonology",b="Blood elves grind recovered magical curios into Glittering Dust, a refined powder unlike common enchanting residue. Their unusual method has caught Archmage Xylem’s curiosity. Higher on the camp’s ridges lies a Kaldorei Tome of Summoning. It reveals more than an interest in Highborne history: the blood elves are willing to summon demons directly into Azshara’s ruins.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are blood elves here in Azshara?",a="Magus Rimtori leads the blood elf excavation across Kalimdor to recover potent magical artifacts from ancient ruins. After the Sunwell’s destruction, they seek power to harvest and siphon.",al={"why are there blood elves in azshara","thalassian base camp purpose","who lives here"}},{q="Why is the Horde hostile to this camp?",a="Magus Rimtori took Horde coin and resources in exchange for a share of the expedition’s discoveries. Once her forces were established in northern Azshara, she broke the agreement and refused tribute. The Horde now seeks revenge.",al={"why do horde attack thalassian base camp","magus rimtori betrayal","betrayed quest lore"}},{q="Who leads the Thalassian Base Camp?",a="Magus Rimtori leads the expedition, though she often travels across Azshara with personal bodyguards. When she is away, Magister Hawkhelm commands the camp.",al={"who is in charge","camp boss","magister hawkhelm"}},{q="What is Glittering Dust?",a="Glittering Dust is arcane residue made by crushing enchanted relics with a specialized blood elf method. Its properties differ from ordinary dust gathered through disenchanting, and the eccentric Archmage Xylem is keenly interested.",al={"magic dust xylem","glittering dust lore","why crush magical items"}},{q="What is the Kaldorei Tome of Summoning on the ridge?",a="The ancient Kaldorei Tome of Summoning rests on a ridge overlooking the camp and can call demons into the area. Its presence shows Rimtori’s expedition pursues darker aims than recovering history.",al={"book on the hill","kaldorei tome","demon book azshara"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde does not take broken oaths lightly. Magus Rimtori took your coin and resources, then answered her promise to share discoveries with treachery. The camp is now a target for retribution.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find the blood elves’ method of refining artifacts into Glittering Dust a rare and dangerous glimpse of Thalassian techniques. Even the eccentric Archmage Xylem is interested."},kw={"azshara","betrayed","glittering dust","hawkhelm","magister hawkhelm","magus rimtori","rimtori","thalassian base camp","ursolan"},rel={"npc:magus-rimtori","zone:azshara","npc:archmage-xylem","subzone:ursolan","topic:horde"},src={"Thalassian Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-eldara"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Eldara",z="azshara",s="At Azshara’s far northeastern edge, the Tower of Eldara keeps its sealed doors above the Bay of Storms. Though long abandoned, its stone endured the Sundering, while beasts prowl the coast below.",h="At Azshara’s far northeastern edge, the Tower of Eldara keeps its sealed doors above the Bay of Storms.",sec={{t="A Relic of Ancient Azshara",b="On a remote cliff northeast of the Bay of Storms, the Tower of Eldara recalls the kaldorei empire that once ruled this coast. Like other ruins in Azshara, it fell into disuse after the Great Sundering. Its entrance remains barred, revealing nothing of the chambers or relics within.\n\nAlong the surrounding shores, murlocs wander, makrura claw across the rocks, and hydras hunt. Few travelers dare approach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Eldara?",a="The Tower of Eldara rises from a northeastern cliff in Azshara, overlooking the Bay of Storms. Built before the Great Sundering, it belonged to the kaldorei empire that once spanned the region.",al={"tower of eldara lore","what is this tower","eldara tower"}},{q="Can you enter the Tower of Eldara?",a="No. The Tower of Eldara remains sealed against outsiders. Its chambers and vaults are barred to explorers.",al={"can i go inside tower of eldara","how to open tower of eldara","is the tower open"}},{q="What threats wander around the tower?",a="Murlocs, armored makrura, and coastal hydras prowl the rocky bluffs and nearby sandy beaches around the promontory.",al={"mobs near tower of eldara","enemies around eldara","bay of storms creatures"}},{q="Where exactly is the tower located?",a="The Tower of Eldara stands on the far eastern tip of land jutting into the Great Sea, just northeast across the Bay of Storms in Azshara.",al={"tower of eldara location","where is tower of eldara","how to find eldara"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Tower of Eldara recalls the grand empire your ancestors ruled before Queen Azshara and the Highborne shattered the ancient world.",["class:Mage"]="Like many Highborne structures across Azshara, the sealed tower may once have echoed with arcane studies before it was locked away from mortal meddling."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","eldara","highborne","kaldorei","ruins","tower of eldara"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:bay-of-storms","topic:murloc"},src={"Tower of Eldara"}}
E["subzone:ursolan"] = {t="subzone",n="Ursolan",z="azshara",s="In western Azshara, Ursolan shelters the Timbermaw furbolgs east of Timbermaw Hold. Its ravine cuts through a stronghold named for the bear Ancient Ursol, where uncorrupted furbolgs defend their ground.",h="In western Azshara, Ursolan shelters the Timbermaw furbolgs east of Timbermaw Hold.",sec={{t="Bastion of the Bear",b="Across a deep ravine in western Azshara, Ursolan climbs both rims. The Timbermaw hold this eastern branch of their territory. Through Timbermaw Hold, it links to Bear's Head in the south.\n\nThe camp takes its name from the bear Ancient Ursol. Here, furbolgs who have resisted the demonic corruption consuming many of their kin across Kalimdor have found a haven. They guard their borders against outsiders, including researchers from the night elven camp of Talrendis.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Ursolan?",a="The Timbermaw furbolgs live in Ursolan. Their tribe is among the few in Kalimdor to resist demonic corruption.",al={"who is at ursolan","ursolan inhabitants","ursolan furbolgs"}},{q="Why is this area called Ursolan?",a="Ursolan honors Ursol, one of the twin bear demigods the furbolgs revere.",al={"ursolan name origin","who is ursolan named after","meaning of ursolan"}},{q="What is the deep gorge running through the camp?",a="A deep ravine cuts through Ursolan. Talrendis biologists from the nearby night elven camp often conduct field studies there.",al={"canyon in ursolan","ravine in ursolan","chasm ursolan"}},{q="How does Ursolan connect to the rest of the Timbermaw territory?",a="Ursolan lies just east of the Azshara entrance to Timbermaw Hold. Mountain tunnels link the Timbermaw's northern presence to Bear's Head in the south.",al={"ursolan connection","how to get to timbermaw hold from ursolan"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can recognize how Ursolan's people revere the twin bear Ancients, Ursol and Ursoc. Both are central to nature worship and mastery of bear form.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere the bear Ancients, yet tensions mark this ground. Talrendis researchers study the ravine under the furbolgs' wary eyes."},kw={"azshara","furbolg","ravine","talrendis","timbermaw","ursol","ursolan"},rel={"subzone:timbermaw-hold","topic:furbolg","subzone:bear-s-head","zone:azshara"},src={"Ursolan"}}
E["subzone:valormok"] = {t="subzone",n="Valormok",z="azshara",s="Valormok keeps a Horde foothold in northwest Azshara. North of the Haldarr Encampment, the outpost sends scouts and travelers toward the cursed ancient ruins along the coast.",h="Valormok keeps a Horde foothold in northwest Azshara.",sec={{t="A Precarious Foothold",b="Autumn-colored trees ring Valormok, where the Horde holds a foothold in a hostile and largely forsaken land. Nearby satyrs, nagas, and prowling beasts threaten the lightly fortified camp. Its warriors hold their ground despite the danger. Wind riders connect Valormok with Orgrimmar and the wilder reaches of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Treachery and Retribution",b="Ag'tor Bloodfist leads Valormok's survivors after Magus Rimtori betrayed their escort. Belgrom Rockmaul sent Horde warriors with the blood elf to seek ancient treasures and powerful relics among the ruins. Rimtori turned on them and killed the warriors to claim the artifacts. Now the survivors plot vengeance against Rimtori and her cohort at the nearby Thalassian Base Camp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Valormok?",a="Valormok is a remote Horde outpost in northwest Azshara. Its flight master connects travelers with routes across Kalimdor, and the camp supports those surveying the ancient coastal wilderness.",al={"valormok azshara","what is this camp","horde base in azshara"}},{q="Who leads the encampment?",a="Ag'tor Bloodfist leads Valormok and maintains the Horde foothold there.",al={"who is in charge","valormok leader","agtor bloodfist"}},{q="Why were so many Horde warriors killed here?",a="Belgrom Rockmaul sent Horde warriors to escort Magus Rimtori as she searched for relics. Rimtori betrayed and killed them to claim the artifacts for herself.",al={"what happened to the guards","valormok massacre","rimtori betrayal"}},{q="Where does the flight master connect to?",a="Valormok's wind rider master offers routes to Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, Splintertree Post, Bloodvenom Post, and Everlook.",al={"valormok flight paths","where can i fly from valormok"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you find a foothold at Valormok among Azshara's treacherous ruins, with flight connections and a call for vengeance.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc stationed far from Orgrimmar, you face a grim test of endurance and bear the duty to avenge your betrayed kin."},kw={"ag'tor bloodfist","azshara","belgrom rockmaul","flight master","jediga","magus rimtori","valormok"},rel={"zone:azshara","npc:magus-rimtori","subzone:thalassian-base-camp","subzone:haldarr-encampment","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:bloodvenom-post","topic:horde"},src={"Valormok"}}
E["topic:cenarius"] = {t="topic",n="Cenarius",z="azshara",s="Across Kalimdor, Cenarius guards the wild places and teaches the night elves druidism. The ancient demigod, son of Elune and Malorne, guided mortal druids for thousands of years before falling in battle during the Third War.",h="Across Kalimdor, Cenarius guards the wild places and teaches the night elves druidism.",sec={{t="Son of Heaven and Earth",b="Born to Elune, goddess of the moon, and Malorne, the great white stag demigod, Cenarius was bound to the mortal world and placed in Malorne's care. Ysera the Dreamer took him as a foster son and guided him along the infinite paths of the Emerald Dream. Cenarius held power over living wood and earth. He fathered the Keepers of the Grove and the dryads, binding his bloodline to Kalimdor's wild places.",sp=0},{t="The First Druid",b="Millennia ago, Malfurion Stormrage, his twin Illidan, and Tyrande Whisperwind sought the legendary demigod. Cenarius saw Malfurion's exceptional heart and trained him as the first mortal druid. When Queen Azshara and her Highborne unleashed the Burning Legion in the War of the Ancients, Cenarius gathered Kalimdor's wild demigods to fight beside the mortal defenders.",sp=0},{t="The Fall at Ashenvale",b="For ten thousand years after the Great Sundering, Cenarius watched over Kalimdor and nurtured the Cenarion Circle with Malfurion. During the Third War, the Warsong clan began cutting timber in Ashenvale. Angered by the ruin of sacred woodlands, Cenarius drove the invaders back.\n\nThen Grom Hellscream and his warriors took Mannoroth's demonic blood. Filled with demonic fury, the corrupted orcs overwhelmed Cenarius and struck him down. Nature's defenders were left in deep sorrow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cenarius?",a="Cenarius is the ancient demigod who guarded Azeroth's wilderness and guided druids. Elune, goddess of the moon, and Malorne, the demigod, were his parents; Ysera fostered him.",al={"who is cenarius","cenarius lore","cenarius backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Who are Cenarius's children?",a="Cenarius fathered the Keepers of the Grove, including Keeper Remulos and Ordanus, and the dryads. The centaur trace their lineage to his son Zaetar, making Cenarius their grandfather.",al={"cenarius children","keepers of the grove father","cenarius daughters"},sp=1,bt={"q1195.3"}},{q="How did Malfurion learn druidism from Cenarius?",a="Before the War of the Ancients, Malfurion sought Cenarius with Illidan and Tyrande. Cenarius recognized Malfurion's rare dedication and balance, then taught him the arts of nature and made him the first mortal druid.",al={"malfurion first druid","how did malfurion learn druidism"}},{q="What happened to Cenarius in the Third War?",a="During the Third War, the Warsong clan cut timber in Ashenvale, drawing Cenarius's wrath. Grom Hellscream drank from a pool tainted by Mannoroth's blood, gained demonic strength, and slew the demigod.",al={"how did cenarius die","who killed cenarius","cenarius death"}},{q="What is Cenarius's connection to the tauren?",a="Tauren druids follow the path Cenarius taught Malfurion Stormrage. Through Hamuul Runetotem's place in the Cenarion Circle, the tauren study Cenarius's ways alongside the night elves.",al={"tauren cenarius","did cenarius teach tauren"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle is an order of druids devoted to preserving nature's balance, studying the Emerald Dream, and guarding sacred forests. Malfurion Stormrage founded it in Cenarius's honor.",al={"what is cenarion circle","who founded cenarion circle"},it="allies"},{q="Where did Cenarius come from?",a="Cenarius was born from the union of Elune, the moon goddess, and the white stag demigod Malorne. Because he belonged more to the mortal realm than the heavens, Elune yielded his upbringing to Malorne and Ysera the Dreamer. Ysera raised Cenarius within the Emerald Dream, tutoring him in its deep mysteries. Over millennia, the Lord of the Forest wandered Azeroth's wilds, teaching the natural ways to ancient peoples and standing beside mortal defenders through catastrophic conflicts like the War of the Ancients.",al={"cenarius origin","cenarius history","birth of cenarius"},it="history",add="19f1e731"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, your path traces back to Cenarius. His lessons to Malfurion established the druidic ways.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere Cenarius as a divine guide and ally. His death at the hands of the Warsong orcs remains an unforgiven tragedy.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor Cenarius's teachings and walk his path alongside the night elves of the Cenarion Circle.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Cenarius's slaying by Grom Hellscream recalls the blood curse and the cost of demonic servitude."},kw={"ashenvale","cenarion","cenarius","druid","elune","malfurion","malorne","remulos","ysera"},rel={"npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:elune","npc:remulos","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:emerald-dream","quest:1088"},src={"Cenarius"}}
E["zone:azshara"] = {t="zone",n="Azshara",z="azshara",s="Along northeastern Kalimdor, Azshara’s broken coast runs from autumn woods to drowned ruins and perilous waters. Horde and Alliance outposts stand near its borders, while naga, ghosts, and other dangers haunt the land.",h="Along northeastern Kalimdor, Azshara’s broken coast runs from autumn woods to drowned ruins and perilous...",sec={{t="A Drowned Empire",b="Zin-Azshari’s coast once lay at the heart of kaldorei civilization. Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara and her Highborne court drew the Burning Legion into Azeroth. So began the War of the Ancients. The Well of Eternity collapsed and the sea swallowed most of the magnificent city. Fractured cliffs, perilous coral reefs, and waterlogged spires remain. Survivors named the ruined land for their fallen monarch, whose pride and betrayal changed it forever.",sp=0},{t="Autumn Splendor and Hidden Perils",b="Crimson, orange, and gold leaves cover Azshara’s woods through an autumn that never ends. Yet the quiet canopy hides a harsh wilderness. Satyrs perform dark rituals in forest hollows, Highborne apparitions haunt drowned foundations, and Spitelash naga prowl the Coral Sea’s shallow reefs. Ferocious beasts, giant hydras, and mountain giants roam the highlands and ivory beaches.",sp=0},{t="A Realm of Exiles and Outcasts",b="Azshara’s isolation and harsh terrain draw those who pursue forgotten crafts or watch dangerous powers. Archmage Xylem lives in a secluded tower high above the cliffs. There, he tests promising spellcasters and cunning rogues. Farther along the coast, the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes watches the waves from a barren isle. At a temple above the churning waters, the immense sea giant Lord Arkkoroc demands blood sacrifices.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are all the trees red and orange here?",a="Azshara’s woods wear crimson, orange, and gold leaves through an endless autumn. The canopy never sheds them, and this striking, melancholy sight has lasted for thousands of years.",al={"why is azshara autumn","why are trees red","azshara fall foliage"}},{q="How did Azshara become a ruin?",a="The coast once formed the outskirts of Zin-Azshari, the kaldorei capital. During the War of the Ancients, the Well of Eternity imploded in the Great Sundering. The continent broke, and vast parts of the city sank beneath the sea.",al={"what happened to azshara","why is azshara broken","azshara history"}},{q="Who rules Azshara today?",a="Neither faction rules all of Azshara. The Alliance keeps a small watch at Talrendis Point near Ashenvale, and the Horde operates from Valormok. Dangerous Spitelash naga, violent satyrs, and untamed monsters dominate the surrounding land.",al={"who controls azshara","who runs azshara","is azshara alliance or horde"}},{q="Who is Archmage Xylem?",a="Archmage Xylem is an eccentric human sorcerer in a remote tower overlooking Azshara’s cliffs. He keeps apart from regional politics and guides visiting mages and rogues through trials that unlock their martial and arcane potential.",al={"xylem azshara","mage tower azshara","wizard in azshara"}},{q="What is the blue dragon doing in the ruins?",a="Azuregos and his brood watch over Eldarath’s ancient ruins. The great blue dragon fiercely guards the powerful Highborne magical artifacts buried in the rubble from mortal hands.",al={"azuregos in azshara","blue dragon azshara","dragon in eldarath"}},{q="Why do the night elves consider this land cursed?",a="The kaldorei consider Azshara cursed because it bears Queen Azshara’s name and architectural legacy. Her pact with the Burning Legion shattered their empire and brought ruin to the world.",al={"is azshara cursed","why do night elves hate azshara","night elf curse azshara"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see drowned pillars and wailing Highborne shades. They recall Queen Azshara’s reckless arrogance and the ruin of the ancient kaldorei civilization.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you find forgotten Highborne sorcery crackling through Eldarath’s shattered stones. High above the cliffs, Archmage Xylem tests those who seek mastery of arcane teleportation and spellcraft.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you find precious veins in Azshara’s steep coastal cliffs and jagged ridges. Mithril, Truesilver, and Thorium are abundant.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you find rare, potent herbs sustained by Azshara’s endless autumn. They include Dreamfoil, Golden Sansam, Mountain Silversage, and Purple Lotus among the ruins."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","bay of storms","coral sea","eldarath","highborne","spitelash","talrendis point","valormok","xylem"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:bay-of-storms","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:lake-mennar","zone:winterspring"},src={"Azshara (Classic)","Azshara"}}
